  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level from all outcomes, then comparing how often each lottery exceeds this level. This involves both averaging outcomes and assessing probabilities of outperforming that average. The individual’s report does not mention any such calculation or reference point. While both the reason and the individual consider probabilities, the reason relies on a specific cognitive mechanism (aspiration level and positive deviations) that is not reflected in the verbal report. The individual’s justification is too vague and generic—focusing only on B seeming better probabilistically—without evidence of the structured evaluation required by the reason. There is no indication that the individual computed or used the mean of all outcomes as a reference point. Therefore, it is unlikely the specific aspiration-level-based reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
